# CC OUT ALL under load (fm1-x0x#15): two dozen lanes changing every block want far more CCs than USB
# takes; the lanes get at most 4 a block, and only while the out queue keeps room for the notes, so no note
# is lost. The computer here takes 300 packets a second (a slow host).
wait 300
tap GLO
turn SELECT 1
turn ALGO 1
turn SELECT 6
turn ALGO 2
tap GLO
wait 100
expect ccoutset 2
# the 909's BD on every step, its notes out on channel 10
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w1
tapkey w2
tapkey w3
tapkey w4
tapkey w5
tapkey w6
tapkey w7
tapkey w8
tapkey w9
tapkey w10
tapkey w11
tapkey w12
tapkey w13
tapkey w14
tapkey w15
# every pot of both 303s: a lane from 0 to 127 and back on every step (a ramp every block)
lanefill 2 0 0 0 127
lanefill 2 0 1 0 127
lanefill 2 0 2 0 127
lanefill 2 0 3 0 127
lanefill 2 0 4 0 127
lanefill 2 0 5 0 127
lanefill 2 0 6 0 127
lanefill 2 0 7 0 127
lanefill 2 0 8 0 127
lanefill 2 0 9 0 127
lanefill 2 0 10 0 127
lanefill 2 0 11 0 127
lanefill 2 1 0 0 127
lanefill 2 1 1 0 127
lanefill 2 1 2 0 127
lanefill 2 1 3 0 127
lanefill 2 1 4 0 127
lanefill 2 1 5 0 127
lanefill 2 1 6 0 127
lanefill 2 1 7 0 127
lanefill 2 1 8 0 127
lanefill 2 1 9 0 127
lanefill 2 1 10 0 127
lanefill 2 1 11 0 127
# and the mixer: each part's level (two CCs each: its 7 and 102-106)
lanefill 5 0 0 20 120
lanefill 5 1 0 20 120
lanefill 5 2 0 20 120
lanefill 5 3 0 20 120
lanefill 5 4 0 20 120
midirate 300
midiclear
tap PLAY
wait 4000
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect notedrops 0
expect noteons >20
expect ccouts >100
expect ccblockmax <5
